# Response headers for Cloudflare Workers Static Assets.
#
# How this file gets where it needs to be: TanStack Start's Vite build emits
# the client bundle into dist/client, and Vite copies everything in public/
# into that directory verbatim (https://vite.dev/guide/assets#the-public-directory).
# The Cloudflare Vite plugin then serves dist/client as the Worker's static
# assets and reads `_headers` from its root at deploy time; the file itself is
# never uploaded as an asset.
#
# Scope: these rules only apply to files served from the assets directory.
# They never touch responses produced by the Worker, i.e. pages rendered by
# TanStack Start or its server routes. Those set headers in code, through the
# `headers` option on a route (see src/routes/_site.essay.$slug.tsx) or on the
# Response a server route returns.
#
# Why only /assets: Vite fingerprints every file under /assets
# (index-<hash>.js, <font>-<hash>.woff2, …), so a new build always produces
# new URLs and the old ones can be cached indefinitely. Everything else in
# public/ (og/*.png, images/**, icons) keeps Cloudflare's default
# `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` plus an ETag, which is what the
# previous deployment served for the same files.
#
# References:
# - https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/
# - https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/vite-plugin/reference/static-assets/
# - https://tanstack.com/start/latest/docs/framework/react/guide/hosting (Cloudflare Workers)
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
